ecution and UI on the client."],[368,"Stops GTA spawning parked traffic on a lift platform."],[548,"Store a Vehicle"],[210,"Store Nearby"],[525,"Suggestions come from `qbx_garages` on Qbox and from `QBCore.Shared.Garages` on QBCore. On ESX and ox\\_core you can type any storage name yourself."],[416,"Supported Frameworks"],[415,"Supported frameworks and how to customize a bridge."],[213,"Terminal"],[251,"Text next to the logo. Wrap a word in `**` to make it bold."],[603,"The brand, the settings and the lift recovery journal are stored against the resource name. A renamed folder starts without them."],[420,"The bridge files are **not escrowed**, so you can point them at your own economy, key script or database layout."],[121,"The client `preparation` function runs for **every group member**."],[239,"The colour, logo and name shown on every terminal and in the Garage Manager. These can also be changed in game under `/evgarage` > **Brand**."],[70,"The FD Laptop is an in-game UI resource that gives players tools based on their job or permission level. It has a customizable interface and works with every major framework."],[528,"The fee is taken from the player's **bank**, and from their **cash** when the bank can't cover it. On ox\\_core it is taken as the `money` item. The car only leaves once the fee is paid."],[412,"The following function is available on the **client thread**, for example to open the Garage Manager from your own admin menu."],[480,"The Garage Manager is where you build and look after your garages. There is no garage list in `config.lua`: every garage is created in game and saved instantly, **no restart needed**."],[518,"The ground under the lift must be level. The allowed difference can be raised under **Settings** > **Advanced**, see Configuration."],[126,"The main data structures used throughout the resource."],[541,"The meaning, default and limits of each value are listed on the Configuration page."],[56,"The missions that ship with the resource, as configured under **Admin** > **Missions**. See Custom Missions to add your own steps."],[100,"The new system may use a different progression formula. Balance the imported data with these values in &#x2A;*`config.lua`**:"],[413,"The other exports you may find in the resource (`SetGarages`, `UpdateStatus`, `RegisterGarageAdapter`, `DrawLighting`, ...) are used internally between the lift and the terminal and are **not** meant to be used by other scripts. Most of them refuse calls from other resources."],[49,"The out of the box configuration for Evolent Boosting."],[158,"The out of the box configuration for Evolent Fleamarket."],[419,"The script talks to your framework through one **bridge file** per framework in `modules/creator/bridge/`. With `Framework = 'auto'` the bridge of the framework that is running is loaded, and the others stay inactive."],[558,"The shutters open and the platform brings the car up from below. The keys are handed over automatically when your key script is supported (see Frameworks)."],[482,"The start screen lists **Your Garages** and gives you three buttons: **Add new garage**, **Brand** and **Settings**."],[516,"The terminal must be **2.5 to 20 metres** from the lift centre, and **outside** the lift footprint and its safety margin."],[567,"The vehicle must fit inside the lift cabin: at most **2.85 m wide**, **6.25 m long** and **2.80 m high**. Larger vehicles are refused with *This vehicle does not fit inside the lift*."],[604,"There are **no SQL files to run**. The script uses the vehicle table your framework already has."],[5,"These commands are restricted to users with the right permissions."],[598,"These resources are **optional**:"],[54,"These settings live in `config.lua` and need a resource restart after a change."],[96,"This guide moves existing player progression (levels, reputation and stats) from **RAHE Boosting** into the Evolent Boosting database."],[97,"This is a one-time data operation that can't easily be undone. Run it while your server is **empty** or the boosting resource is **stopped**, and make a database backup first."],[159,"This is the out of the box `config.lua`. Adjust the framework, inventory and categories to fit your server."],[219,"This is the out of the box `config.lua`. Times are in **milliseconds**, distances in **metres**."],[411,"This page documents the functions exported by our resource that other scripts may use."],[555,"This page explains how players use a garage, so you know what to expect and what to tell your community."],[182,"This page lists all available in-game commands."],[526,"Tick **Impound garage** and set a **Release fee** to turn a garage into an impound."],[513,"Tick **On duty only** to require players to be on duty for one of the listed jobs."],[266,"Time the lift takes to lower (2000 - 60000)."],[263,"Time the lift takes to rise (2000 - 60000)."],[272,"Time the shutters take to open or close (500 - 30000)."],[294,"Time to drive a collected car off the lift. After that it goes back into storage."],[297,"Time to drive onto the lift when storing. After that the lift lowers empty."],[593,"Tired of invisible parking spots and cars popping out of thin air? Yeah, us too. That’s why we built real underground garages.\nPlayers walk up to a terminal, pick a car, and watch an animated lift bring it up from below. Everything is placed and managed in game, no config editing needed."],[140,"Tired of the same old point A to B boosts? Yeah, us too. That’s why we built a next-level boosting system.\nOur system is packed with variety, real progression, and features that actually make sense."],[572,"To your impound garage. The player is told *A vehicle of yours was recovered and taken to the impound*. With no impound garage, it behaves like `'last'`."],[216,"Translate the values"],[623,"Type"],[628,"Type"],[643,"Type"],[652,"Type"],[661,"Type"],[668,"Type"],[675,"Type"],[684,"Type"],[691,"Type"],[125,"Types"],[591,"Updating"],[7,"Usage example"],[40,"Usage example"